{"id":"q21","run":1,"role":"calibration","category":"probability","question":"Is the expected number of rolls of a fair six-sided die needed to see all six faces at least once greater than 14?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":null,"claims":[{"text":"The expected number of rolls to see all six faces is 14.7.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"14.7 is greater than 14, so the answer is yes.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"With i faces seen, the expected wait for a new face is 6/(6-i).","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The total expectation is the sum of stage waits: 1+1.2+1.5+2+3+6.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The expectation equals 6H_6 with H_6 = 49/20.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The stage-by-stage argument and the harmonic formula agree, so the value is reliable.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The margin of 0.7 is small, so an arithmetic slip could flip the comparison.","confidence":0.15,"lean":-1,"theta":0.2356,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The median number of rolls is about 13, below the mean, so many runs finish in 14 or fewer rolls.","confidence":0.7,"lean":-1,"theta":1.0996,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The median concerns the distribution, not the expectation, so it does not change the answer.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":8,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":4,"J":0.7,"re